    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="72c02e6d-8c15-5d93-ac0a-dbff23f6970d" activityNameId="c0ede3bb-5e2b-5cd5-bee1-c439f72c586e" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Use, computer, laptop, standby/sleep mode</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Use, computer, laptop, standby/sleep mode
The laptop use in the standby/sleep mode includes the share of the laptop computer production, the energy consumption (use-phase) for the laptop (incl. monitor) and the rail and road transport from factory to user. Energy consumption of laptop computers (use-phase) vary a lot depending on the device looked at. Min.-Max. values are listed;
Synonyms: Notebook, Lifebook; 
UUID: cc2e7bee-80b7-35da-a651-9ba551b7248a
Describes the use of a laptop computer in the standby/sleep mode. Calculated per 1 hour of laptop use. Laptop computer life span assumed to be 4 years. Standby/sleep mode 2 hours a day (office use), 240 days a year. Swiss supply mix applied for electricity consumption (low voltage).
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: No technology involved, except for the production of the laptop computer, which is described in another dataset.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Manufacturers, literature and own assumptions. 
Extrapolations: see Geography and Technology
Uncertainty adjustments: International data suitable for Switzerland.
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_cc2e7bee-80b7-35da-a651-9ba551b7248a.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
